        "name": "Craig Topper",
        "email": "craig.topper@sifive.com",
        "date": "2026-03-17T22:28:06Z"
      },
      "message": "Update (P)SATI assembly mnemonic to use uimm+1. Bump version to 0.20\n\nThis matches the opinion on this thread https://lists.riscv.org/g/tech-p-ext/message/927\n\nVersion bump is so I can implement this in LLVM and note it as a\nbackwards incompatible change.\n\nI've update the descriptions for (P)SATI/(P)USATI to use 'width' in\nplace of 'n'. 'width' is defined as 'uimm'+1 for (P)SATI and\n'uimm' for (P)USATI. I'm open to further suggestions on how to make\nthis as clear as possible.",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "e9c2b7df2863787b978468218e4b45b6e0a17a6f",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/riscv/riscv-p-spec/git/trees/e9c2b7df2863787b978468218e4b45b6e0a17a6f"
